To modify your NGINX configuration for SSL using your own certificates (instead of Let's Encrypt), you can update the `ssl_certificate` and `ssl_certificate_key` directives with the paths to your own certificate and key files. 

In your case, you have files like `commercial.crt`, `private.key`, etc. Here's how you can modify the configuration:

```nginx
# Odoo server upstream configurations
upstream bastdotmydotid {
    server 103.193.179.189:8069;
}
upstream bastdotmydotidchat {
    server 103.193.179.189:8072;
}

# http -> https redirection
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name bast.my.id;
    rewrite ^(.*) https://$host$1 permanent;
}

map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name bast.my.id;
    proxy_read_timeout 720s;
    proxy_connect_timeout 720s;
    proxy_send_timeout 720s;
    client_max_body_size 100M;

    # Add Headers for odoo proxy mode
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;

    # SSL parameters (using your own certificates)
    ssl_certificate /home/evan/commercial.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /home/evan/private.key;

    # log paths
    access_log /var/log/nginx/bastdotmydotid.access.log;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/bastdotmydotid.error.log;

    # Redirect longpoll requests to odoo longpolling port
    location /longpolling {
        proxy_pass http://bastdotmydotidchat;
    }

    # Redirect requests to odoo backend server
    location / {
        # Add Headers for odoo proxy mode
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_redirect off;
        proxy_pass http://bastdotmydotid;
        add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains";
        # Uncomment if your nginx version supports this:
        # proxy_cookie_flags session_id samesite=lax secure;
    }

    # WebSocket handling
    location /websocket {
        proxy_pass http://bastdotmydotidchat;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;

        add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains";
        # Uncomment if your nginx version supports this:
        # proxy_cookie_flags session_id samesite=lax secure;
    }

    # common gzip configuration
    gzip_types text/css text/scss text/plain text/xml application/xml application/json application/javascript;
    gzip on;
}
```

### Key Changes:
- Updated `ssl_certificate` and `ssl_certificate_key` paths to your custom SSL certificate files: `commercial.crt` and `private.key`.
- Removed references to Let's Encrypt.

Make sure your certificates are in the correct format (`.crt` for the certificate and `.key` for the private key). You may also want to include intermediate CA certificates if required.

After modifying the configuration, test the NGINX configuration with:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

If everything is correct, reload NGINX:

```bash
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

