Here is an updated NGINX configuration to handle the CSRF verification properly, especially when running your application behind a reverse proxy. This configuration ensures that the necessary headers are passed from NGINX to your application for proper CSRF handling.

```nginx
# Odoo server upstream configurations
upstream mapdotportal {
    server 160.22.193.9:8001;
}

# http -> https redirection
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name map.exatel.co.id;
    rewrite ^(.*) https://$host$1 permanent;
}

map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name map.exatel.co.id;
    proxy_read_timeout 720s;
    proxy_connect_timeout 720s;
    proxy_send_timeout 720s;
    client_max_body_size 100M;

    # Add Headers for odoo proxy mode
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;  # Important for CSRF

    # SSL parameters (using your own certificates)
    ssl_certificate /home/evan/commercial.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /home/evan/private.key;

    # log paths
    access_log /var/log/nginx/map.access.log;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/map.error.log;

    # Redirect requests to odoo backend server
    location / {
        # Add Headers for odoo proxy mode
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;  # Important for CSRF
        proxy_redirect off;
        proxy_pass http://mapdotportal;
        add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains";
        # Uncomment if your nginx version supports this:
        # proxy_cookie_flags session_id samesite=lax secure;
    }

    # common gzip configuration
    gzip_types text/css text/scss text/plain text/xml application/xml application/json application/javascript;
    gzip on;
}
```

### Key Additions:
- **`proxy_set_header Host $host;`**: This ensures that the correct `Host` header is passed to the upstream application, which is important for CSRF validation in frameworks like Django or Odoo.
- **Other Essential Headers**: Make sure headers such as `X-Real-IP`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, and `Host` are included for the reverse proxy setup.

### Additional Considerations:
1. **CSRF Token in Forms**: Ensure that your web application's forms or API requests include a valid CSRF token.
2. **HTTPS Setup**: Ensure your SSL certificates are correctly configured and that HTTPS is enforced.

After applying this updated NGINX configuration, restart NGINX:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

