/* styles/globals.css or styles/app.css */
@import '~@dilrukr/react-text-scramble/build/scramble.css';
```

This way, Next.js should apply the styles without issues.

### 2. **Import CSS in `_app.tsx` (Next.js Custom App)**

Alternatively, you can directly import the CSS in your `_app.tsx` file. In Next.js, this file is used to wrap all pages and components, making it an ideal place to import global styles:

```tsx
// pages/_app.tsx or _app.js

import '../styles/globals.css'; // Your global styles
import '@dilrukr/react-text-scramble/build/scramble.css'; // Import scramble.css

